course: dictionary
lesson: 7795
title: Quantitative: numbers and amounts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Quantitative is a long word, but it is about something you already know: amounts. A quantity is how much or how many of something. So quantitative means to do with amounts, numbers, or things you can measure or count.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «The plant grew 5 cm» gives a number and a unit, cm, so it is a measured amount. Ask yourself: can I count it or measure it? If yes, quantitative probably fits.
explain: Some things are not measured in numbers. «The leaves turned yellow» describes a colour, not an amount. In science, measured numbers are called quantitative data, and descriptions are called qualitative data.
explain: The word also appears in money. «Quantitative easing» means the central bank, the country's own bank in charge of its money, creating new money. The word still points to amounts: the bank changes how much money there is. Check by swapping in "to do with amounts" and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Quantitative means to do with amounts or numbers, things you can measure or count.
fact: Quantitative data are information in numbers, such as heights, times or temperatures.
fact: «The plant grew 5 cm» is quantitative: it gives a measured number with a unit.
fact: Qualitative data are descriptions, such as «the leaves turned yellow».
fact: «Quantitative easing» means the central bank creating new money.
exercise: «The plant grew 5 cm.» Is this quantitative or qualitative? | Qualitative, because it describes how the plant looks | *Quantitative, because it gives a measured number | Neither, because plants cannot grow
exercise: «The leaves turned yellow.» Which kind of data is this? | Quantitative, because it has a unit | *Qualitative, because it is a description | Quantitative, because it is a number
exercise: What does quantitative mean? | To do with colours and pictures | *To do with amounts, numbers, or things you can measure or count | To do with feelings and opinions
test: Give a quantitative answer to: How long is the pencil? | It is a yellow pencil | *It is 15 cm long | Pencils are useful | It is very long
test: Which of these is quantitative data? | A sunny day | *Times, heights or temperatures written as numbers | A story about a dog | Happy faces drawn in class
exam: In «Quantitative easing» the central bank creates new money. What does quantitative mean here? | To do with a shop name | To do with the colour of money | To do with a feeling about money | *To do with the amount of money
